  "goodToKnow": "Die Gedenktafel is a memorial plaque on a building, marking where a famous person lived or an event took place. Related are the Stolpersteine, small brass plaques set into the pavement by artist Gunter Demnig since the 1990s, each naming a victim of Nazi persecution outside their last chosen home; there are now over 100,000 across Europe. Gedenken means to commemorate. Plural: die Gedenktafeln."
